course: dictionary
lesson: 483
title: Artificial: made by people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Artificial means made by people, not made by nature. «Artificial flowers» are not grown in the ground. People make them from plastic or cloth so they look like real ones. Artificial is the opposite of natural.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Artificial flowers are a copy of real flowers, so the word tells you they are not the real thing. Try the swap test: put "made by people" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe behaviour. An «artificial smile» is not sincere, so it is fake. Read the sentence around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Artificial means made by people, not natural.
fact: «Artificial flowers» are a copy of real flowers.
fact: An «artificial smile» is not sincere, so it is fake.
fact: AI means artificial intelligence: computer programs that do tasks like talking, sorting or answering.
fact: On 4 October 1957 the Soviet Union launched Sputnik 1, the first artificial satellite, a machine put in orbit round Earth.
exercise: Mum bought «artificial flowers» for the table. What are they? | *Flowers made by people to look like real ones | Flowers that grow in the sea | Flowers that have no colour | Real flowers picked from the garden
exercise: Sam says the actor's smile was «artificial». What does Sam mean? | *It was fake, not sincere | It was made from wax | It was a real, happy smile | It was very big
exercise: Which of these is an artificial satellite? | A rock falling from space | A bird flying over the sea | *A metal machine people put into orbit round Earth | A moon going round Earth
test: Which word means made by people, not natural? | *Artificial | Wild | Glum | Ancient
test: What does AI stand for, and what is it? | Air Injection, a type of engine | *Artificial intelligence, computer programs that do tasks needing thinking | Any Item, a shop word | Animal Instinct, a kind of pet
exam: «Organic farming uses fewer artificial chemicals.» What does artificial mean here? | Glowing in the dark | Found growing wild | Very old | *Made by people, not natural
